## Verbose output control

- Purpose: coerce models to be terse (code-first, prose-light) during agentic loops.
- Controlled per-model from the **Output Verbosity** dashboard card
  (`GET/PUT /api/verbosity`); defaults: `deepseek-v4-flash` ON, `deepseek-v4-pro` OFF,
  `glm-4.7` ON, `glm-5.3` OFF.
- Three request-side mechanisms — **never edits response content**:
  1. **Directive injection** — appends `flashTersenessDirective` (10 enumerated
     mandatory constraints) to the last system/developer message
  2. **Token cap** — lowers `max_tokens` to model-specific ceiling:
     - `deepseek-v4-flash`: 4096
     - `deepseek-v4-pro`: 8192
     - `glm-4.7`: 8192
     - `glm-5.3` / `glm-5.3[1m]`: 16384
- Verbosity is applied **after** the subagent-router downgrade so the final
  served model determines which controls fire

## Runtime settings (no restart)

| Aspect | Detail |
| ------- | ------ |
| Compression runtime toggles | `GET/PUT /api/settings` in usage UI → applies immediately, no restart |
| Config fields | `ToolCompressionEnabled bool`, `Verbosity map[string]bool`, `ThinkingEnabled map[string]bool` (in `AppSettings`/`LiveSettings`) |
| Tool threshold | `toolResultMaxLen` (4000 chars) |
| Failure / key-missing | Soft failures (empty/not-shorter summary) truncate to `toolResultMaxLen`; hard errors fail-open with original body |

## Global subagent model sizing (flash fleet)

The live subagent fleet lives in `/.cursor/agents/` (10 files).
All agents now use `model: o3-mini` (deepseek-v4-flash) so the high-volume
flash fleet never competes with the main chat's glm-4.7 plan slots (2
concurrent) — cached deepseek turns answer in ~2s vs 20-45s queued on GLM.
Free tier fallback handles peak-hour exhaustion automatically.

| Agent | model: | Rationale |
| ----- | ------ | --------- |
| explore-flash | `o3-mini` | Read-only search/read/cite; high volume |
| browser-flash | `o3-mini` | Read-only fetch + extract + cite |
| web-researcher-flash | `o3-mini` | Read-only search + cite synthesis |
| doc-writer-flash | `o3-mini` | Prose generation from diffs |
| bash-flash | `o3-mini` | Multi-step CLI loops; tool/agentic chops |
| refactor-flash | `o3-mini` | Mechanical, must not break call-sites |
| test-runner-flash | `o3-mini` | Runs tests + simple fixes |
| implementer-flash | `o3-mini` | Writes working code |
| code-reviewer-flash | `o3-mini` | Finds correctness bugs |
| verifier-flash | `o3-mini` | Independent validation |

Keep this table in sync when editing `/.cursor/agents/*.md`.

